# Redford Crossing — Ink and Vellum
; The travelling theme, plus what this map wants of it.
;
; NOTE, and it is a finding rather than an omission: `ford : stroke=`,
; `fill=`, `width=` and `glyph=` are ALL inert. A crossing is drawn as a
; restyled segment of the water's own band with its colours fixed at the draw
; site, so the one feature this map is named for cannot be themed at all. That
; is the same class as #150 and is recorded there.
kind: theme
use: ../ink-and-vellum.theme.cd

[theme]
; The river is the map's subject, so it carries more ink than the base sets.
river : stroke=#4d6f79 width=2.5
